1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"phase-0--0d-enjoy-the-process","kind":"phase-article","route":"/roadmap/phase-0/0d-enjoy-the-process","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/phase-0/0d-enjoy-the-process","sourceHash":"72f805bd3e19420234cfd905b83eea7ebd9558e60e2517b583754e44d4587fc6","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T23:11:34.339Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"0D — Enjoy the Process","zh":"0D — 享受过程"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"segment-0001","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Learning a foreign language takes a lot of hours. A native English speaker learning Spanish will need around 1300-1400 hours to reach a high level of fluency. Spanish is closely related to English, which makes it faster. If your target is something like Russian or Japanese, expect 1700 or 2700+ hours respectively. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/categories-of-language-difficulty\">Categories of Language Difficulty</a>","zh":"学习一门外语需要投入大量时间。以英语为母语的人学习西班牙语，通常需要大约 1300–1400 小时才能达到较高的流利程度。西班牙语与英语关系密切，因此学习速度会更快。如果你的目标语言是俄语或日语之类的语言，预计分别需要 1700 小时或 2700 小时以上。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/categories-of-language-difficulty\">语言难度分类</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0002","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Everyone learns differently and these are only estimates, but the fact remains: no matter how you do the math, it takes a very long time to learn a language.","zh":"每个人的学习方式都不同，这些数字也只是估算，但事实仍然是：无论怎么算，学会一门语言都需要非常漫长的时间。"}},{"id":"the-fun-threshold","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"The Fun Threshold","zh":"乐趣门槛"}},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Most people won't do something they hate for even 50 hours, let alone thousands. If you want to be successful, you must find a way to enjoy language learning.","zh":"大多数人连自己讨厌的事情都做不了 50 个小时，更不用说几千个小时了。如果你想取得成功，就必须找到享受语言学习的方法。"}},{"id":"segment-0005","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"This is why a large part of the Refold method is built around enjoyment. The easiest way to enjoy a new language is to reach what we call the \"fun threshold\" — the point in your journey when you know enough to enjoy the content <em>behind</em> the language.","zh":"这就是为什么 Refold 方法的很大一部分都围绕着享受来构建。享受一门新语言最简单的方法，就是达到我们所说的“乐趣门槛”——也就是在学习过程中，你已经掌握了足够多的内容，能够享受语言<em>背后的</em>内容。"}},{"id":"segment-0006","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Once you're beyond basic comprehension, all you need to do is find things you enjoy. Getting past basic comprehension is the hardest part, but once you can relax with a book, TV show, or podcast, it's mostly downhill from there.","zh":"一旦你超越了基础理解能力，接下来要做的就是找到自己喜欢的内容。突破基础理解是最困难的部分，但当你能够通过书籍、电视节目或播客放松下来时，之后大多就会越来越轻松。"}},{"id":"segment-0007","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"As a beginner, you don't know enough to make sense of anything. Most sentences are gibberish with maybe a few words you recognize. But as you learn more, you start to actually enjoy things — stories, jokes, people's personalities.","zh":"作为初学者，你掌握的内容还不足以理解任何东西。大多数句子听起来都像乱码，可能只有几个词你能认出来。但随着学习深入，你会开始真正享受其中的乐趣——故事、笑话，以及人物的个性。"}},{"id":"getting-through-the-hard-part","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Getting Through the Hard Part","zh":"度过艰难阶段"}},{"id":"segment-0009","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"We understand this, and we try to make the road to the fun threshold enjoyable too — but it's more of a \"Type 2 fun.\" Type 1 fun is fun in the moment: you're laughing and having a great time. Type 2 fun can be difficult or frustrating while it's happening, but afterward you're glad you did it. Putting in the effort to understand a simple sentence in a new language can be quite frustrating in the moment, but afterwards, you get a feeling of accomplishment for pushing yourself to learn more.","zh":"我们理解这一点，也会尽量让通往乐趣门槛的道路变得愉快一些——但这更像是“第二类乐趣”。第一类乐趣是当下就能感受到的乐趣：你在欢笑，享受美好时光。第二类乐趣在经历时可能困难或令人沮丧，但事后你会庆幸自己坚持了下来。努力理解新语言中的一个简单句子，当下可能相当令人沮丧，但之后，当你因为逼迫自己继续学习而获得进步时，又会产生一种成就感。"}},{"id":"segment-0010","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The beginner phases can be tough, especially if you haven't found things you like about learning yet. Framing it as a puzzle or personal challenge can help.","zh":"初学阶段可能很艰难，尤其是当你还没有找到学习中的乐趣时。把它看成一个谜题或个人挑战，可能会有所帮助。"}},{"id":"segment-0011","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"This isn't meant to scare you away — it's meant to prepare you. With the right mindset and approach, anyone can get over the fun threshold and make it to fluency.","zh":"这并不是为了吓退你，而是为了让你做好准备。只要心态和方法正确，任何人都能跨过乐趣门槛，最终达到流利水平。"}},{"id":"research-and-reasoning","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Research and Reasoning","zh":"研究与依据"}},{"id":"segment-0013","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The hour estimates in this article are based on data from the Foreign Service Institute (FSI), which has been teaching languages to American diplomats for decades. Their estimates are frequently miscited — the hours on their website are classroom hours only, but students also do roughly 17 hours per week of self-study on top of 23 hours in class. Our estimates are adapted from the FSI data to better reflect immersion-based learning. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/how-long-does-it-take-to-learn-a-language\">How Long Does It Take to Learn a Language</a>","zh":"本文中的时间估算基于美国外交学院（FSI）的数据。几十年来，FSI 一直在为美国外交官教授语言。FSI 的估算经常被误引——其网站上列出的小时数仅指课堂学习时间，但学生还会在每周 23 小时的课堂学习之外，额外进行大约 17 小时的自学。我们的估算参考了 FSI 的数据，并作了调整，以更好地反映基于沉浸的学习。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/how-long-does-it-take-to-learn-a-language\">学会一门语言需要多长时间</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0014","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The importance of motivation and enjoyment in language learning is well-supported by research. Dörnyei (2005) has written extensively on the psychology of language learner motivation, and the relationship between intrinsic motivation and sustained effort is one of the most robust findings in educational psychology. The \"fun threshold\" concept isn't a formal research term, but it reflects what studies on free voluntary reading (Krashen, 2004; McQuillan, 2019) have shown: learners who find enjoyable content in their target language sustain their effort far longer than those who rely on willpower alone.","zh":"研究充分支持动机和享受在语言学习中的重要性。Dörnyei（2005）对语言学习者动机的心理学进行了大量研究，而内在动机与持续努力之间的关系，是教育心理学中最稳健的研究发现之一。“乐趣门槛”并不是正式的研究术语，但它反映了自由自愿阅读研究（Krashen，2004；McQuillan，2019）所揭示的现象：能够在目标语言中找到有趣内容的学习者，比单纯依靠意志力的学习者更能长久地坚持努力。"}}],"cards":[]},"siteBasePath":"/my_learning_docs"}]
